Every clinician should evaluate a risk for an opioid-related-harm before an opioid-initiation.
Every clinician should evaluate a risk for an opioid-related-harm during a periodic-continuation-review.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should discuss a risk for an opioid-related-harm with the patient.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should incorporate a risk-mitigation-strategy in a management-plan with the patient and should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should review a potential-prescribed-medication-interaction with the patient.
If a clinician uses an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should review a potential-used-substance-interaction with the patient.
